cmd: printenv
args: WINUX_DIFFVAR -0
timeout: 10
source: github.com/unixwin/WinuxCmd/issues/1462
tags: audit-w3b printenv plus-getopt operand-boundary
# The looked-up variable must be one the interop launch shape delivers to
# the Windows subject with the same value the Linux oracle sees. LC_ALL
# (used when the case was written) is pinned only on the WSL side and
# never crosses the interop boundary; SHLVL proved host-shell-nesting
# dependent. The runner exports WINUX_DIFFVAR to both sides and lists it
# in WSLENV (no flag = verbatim sharing), so the subject receives the
# premise by construction.
